1. A light detection and ranging (LiDAR) system comprising:

a light source configured to emit source light;

a first optical splitter disposed in an optical path of the source light and configured to split the source light into a first beam and a second beam;

a beam-dividing assembly configured to divide the second beam into a plurality of sub-beams;

a beam-steering assembly configured to direct the plurality of sub-beams in a plurality of different directions toward an environment; and

a receiver configured to detect return light from the environment resulting from at least one of the first beam or the plurality of sub-beams and to generate signals usable to determine a distance to one or more objects in the environment.

**Apparatus Claim**

1. An optical measurement system comprising:  
   a light source configured to emit an optical beam;  
   a beam splitter positioned to receive the optical beam and divide the optical beam into a first beam and a second beam, the first beam being transmitted along a direct optical path;  
   a beam-dividing assembly configured to divide the second beam into a plurality of measurement beams;  
   a beam-steering assembly configured to selectively direct the plurality of measurement beams toward an object; and  
   an optical receiver configured to receive optical radiation associated with the plurality of measurement beams after interaction with the object and to generate measurement signals representative of at least one characteristic of the object.

1. **An optical ranging apparatus comprising:**

   an optical source configured to generate a source beam comprising optical pulses;

   a beam splitter disposed in an optical path of the source beam and configured to split the source beam into:

   a first split beam propagating along a first optical path; and

   a second split beam propagating along a second optical path different from the first optical path;

   a first transmitting optical assembly arranged in the first optical path and configured to direct at least a portion of the first split beam into a scene as a first transmitted beam;

   a beam-subdivision assembly arranged in the second optical path and configured to subdivide the second split beam into a plurality of third beams;

   a directional-emission assembly optically coupled to the beam-subdivision assembly and configured to emit the plurality of third beams into the scene in a plurality of respective emission directions, at least two of the respective emission directions being different from one another and from an emission direction of the first transmitted beam, such that transmitted beams of the optical ranging apparatus comprise the first transmitted beam derived from the first split beam and the plurality of third beams derived from the second split beam;

   a receiving optical assembly configured to collect return light produced by reflection of at least one of the first transmitted beam or the plurality of third beams from one or more objects in the scene;

   at least one optical detector configured to convert the collected return light into one or more electrical return signals; and

   a processing circuit coupled to the optical source and the at least one optical detector and configured to:

   determine, for each of at least a subset of the first transmitted beam and the plurality of third beams, a time interval between transmission of the corresponding beam and detection of return light associated with the corresponding beam;

   determine a distance to an object based on the time interval; and

   associate the determined distance with the emission direction of the corresponding beam to generate spatially resolved range information for the scene.
